WEBVTT

00:05.520 --> 00:10.110
It's only just turned December, but
the town already looks so Christmassy!

00:10.360 --> 00:11.820
Bring on Christmas!

00:12.110 --> 00:17.740
We have to earn as much as we can from the holiday
rush to pay expenses for our New Year's Eve show.

00:18.200 --> 00:23.170
I've been trying to get in as many
shifts at SuperNova as possible!

00:23.750 --> 00:27.000
Don't work yourself too hard, Suzu.

00:27.210 --> 00:30.300
I'll be fine! I'm sure I can handle it.

00:30.800 --> 00:36.260
Speaking of, you'll be working part-time
at Nico's shopping arcade this year, right?

00:36.560 --> 00:38.769
They're busy with sales or something?

00:38.770 --> 00:41.809
Yeah! I'm helping with the Christmas sales.

00:41.810 --> 00:44.980
Ah! Um, about that...

00:45.900 --> 00:49.399
It looks like things have changed a bit.

00:49.400 --> 00:50.110
Huh?

00:50.400 --> 00:51.990
What do you mean?

00:52.360 --> 00:53.699
Well, you see...

00:53.700 --> 00:56.825
Opening Sale Underway

00:53.700 --> 00:59.950
Christmas Light-Up Display

00:53.700 --> 00:54.990
GIANT
DEPARTMENT

00:54.991 --> 00:59.580
A really big department store recently
opened up near our shopping area.

00:56.826 --> 00:59.950
Free Nationwide Delivery

01:02.620 --> 01:06.420
Kuni. Yasu. This is where it counts.

01:07.000 --> 01:11.340
For the shopping arcade...
that's always been there for us!

01:11.760 --> 01:12.590
Yup!

01:12.591 --> 01:14.430
Yes. Count me in.

01:15.390 --> 01:16.930
Our foe is huge.

01:17.390 --> 01:18.390
But...

01:19.180 --> 01:21.180
GIANT
DEPARTMENT

01:21.181 --> 01:22.230
We CANNOT lose!

01:26.310 --> 01:27.809
Ippai hibiki MUSIC
Ring out, tons of music

01:27.810 --> 01:29.319
Ippai kimari POSING
Do tons of cool posing

01:29.320 --> 01:30.819
Ippai todoke FEELING
Let tons of feelings reach you

01:30.820 --> 01:32.319
Super Soni let's go!
Super Soni let's go!

01:32.320 --> 01:33.779
Suggoi shigeki tenkomori
Stimulation super piling up

01:33.780 --> 01:35.296
Suggoi tama ni karamawari
Sometimes super running in circles

01:35.320 --> 01:36.909
Suggoi kimi to zutto ENJOY
Always super enjoy being with you

01:36.910 --> 01:39.160
Super Soni LET'S GO! Desu
Super Soni let's go! Yes

01:51.130 --> 01:55.590
Saikin omoitsukimashita
Lately, I've come to realize

01:57.220 --> 02:01.560
Kimochi tsutaeru tte taihen
That getting feelings across is tough

02:03.310 --> 02:08.109
Umaku dekitari dekinattari
Whether it goes well or not

02:08.110 --> 02:11.859
Muzukashii kara oku no te de
Is tough, so my trump card

02:11.860 --> 02:14.440
Mouretsu taiatari desu
Is going for it at full force

02:16.200 --> 02:18.490
Dakedo hitomishiri (hitomishiri)
But I'm shy (shy)

02:19.120 --> 02:21.920
Gomakashite senobi (senobi)
I act like it's nothing and aim high (high)

02:22.290 --> 02:23.829
Ashi ga gakuburu de
With legs trembling

02:23.830 --> 02:27.080
Hirakinaotte arinomama GO!
I get serious and just go for it!

02:27.460 --> 02:30.089
Zenkai, soukai, daitenkai Recuperation,
exhilaration, a big revolution

02:30.090 --> 02:33.130
Nandemo chokushin STRAIGHT
No matter what, keep heading straight

02:33.460 --> 02:36.129
Sekai, mankai, mugendai
The world, in full bloom, infinity

02:36.130 --> 02:39.679
Kyou mo genki ni koko ni imasu (HEY!) I'm
here again today, living to the fullest (Hey!)

02:39.680 --> 02:41.196
Ippai hibike MUSIC
Ring out, tons of music

02:41.220 --> 02:42.639
Ippai kimari POSING
Do tons of cool posing

02:42.640 --> 02:44.286
Ippai todoke FEELING?
Let tons of feelings reach you

02:44.310 --> 02:45.559
Super Soni let's go!
Super Soni let's go!

02:45.560 --> 02:47.229
Suggoi shigeki tenkomori
Stimulation super piling up

02:47.230 --> 02:48.559
Suggoi tama ni karamawari
Sometimes super running in circles

02:48.560 --> 02:50.376
Suggoi kimi to zutto ENJOY
Always super enjoy being with you

02:50.400 --> 02:52.570
SUPER SONI LET'S GO! Desu
Super Soni let's go! Yes

02:55.860 --> 02:59.739
Ayaka, what do you want for Christmas?

02:59.740 --> 03:01.300
Ayaka

03:01.301 --> 03:02.580
Uh, well... It's a secret!

03:02.910 --> 03:03.910
Why?

03:04.200 --> 03:08.670
Because I already asked
Santa for it. So it's a secret!

03:08.960 --> 03:11.000
Come on, you can tell me.

03:13.130 --> 03:14.589
A Saint Comes to Town

03:14.590 --> 03:16.420
A secret's a secret!

03:19.590 --> 03:21.260
Christmas Operations Center

03:20.220 --> 03:22.929
Thank you for coming, everyone.

03:21.261 --> 03:22.930
Musatani
Shopping
District
Office

03:22.930 --> 03:30.930
Christmas Festivities Association
TOMI

03:23.600 --> 03:27.559
As you know, the department store
that opened three months ago

03:27.560 --> 03:34.440
has cut into the Musatani Shopping District's
customer base. Sales are down 30% from last year!

03:34.860 --> 03:41.359
If we want to see our way through this, we
MUST make our Christmas sales event a success!

03:41.360 --> 03:42.200
Yeah!

03:42.201 --> 03:43.950
Tomi! You can count on me!

03:44.240 --> 03:45.289
And me, too.

03:45.290 --> 03:47.870
We'll teach that store a lesson!

03:48.210 --> 03:54.290
Thank you, everyone. But we'll be no match
for that store if we do things as usual.

03:54.710 --> 03:58.260
Thus, we've set up a Christmas
Sale Special Task Force!

03:59.260 --> 04:03.350
I will be project leader.
And as special advisor...

03:59.280 --> 04:00.715
Chairman TOMI

04:00.716 --> 04:02.150
Vice-Chairman YASU

04:04.050 --> 04:06.560
I've requested Ms. Suzu Fujimi!

04:08.810 --> 04:13.480
As Mr. Tomi just said,
my name is Suzu Fujimi.

04:14.310 --> 04:19.649
To get right to the point, when investigating the
consumer profile of visitors to the shopping district,

04:19.650 --> 04:22.199
we've seen a drop-off
mainly in the younger ones.

04:22.200 --> 04:25.570
Dept. Store
Reconnaissance

04:22.490 --> 04:25.580
Most of them are being siphoned off
by that department store.

04:26.030 --> 04:30.710
The damage is especially severe for the
book store, toy store, and the boutique.

04:31.040 --> 04:32.120
That's right.

04:32.830 --> 04:36.000
That damn store! Their
selection's okay, but that's it!

04:36.290 --> 04:38.550
What's so great about brand names?!

04:39.210 --> 04:43.129
And so, the young women working
in the shopping arcade...

04:43.130 --> 04:46.050
will all wear these outfits!

04:46.930 --> 04:47.760
Whoa!

04:47.761 --> 04:48.970
That's great!

04:49.310 --> 04:51.940
It makes me feel young, body and mind.

04:52.890 --> 04:53.890
Objection!

04:54.650 --> 04:56.440
Will cosplay of that level...

04:56.860 --> 05:02.780
rather, OBJECTIFICATION of that level actually
bring youngsters back to our shopping district?

05:03.950 --> 05:06.160
These "Santas" are merely the backups.

05:06.910 --> 05:09.869
I have carefully selected
the main ones myself.

05:09.870 --> 05:13.750
These two will be giving
their all in THESE outfits!

05:15.380 --> 05:17.249
I-isn't that Sonico?

05:17.250 --> 05:19.420
That gal next to her is cute, too!

05:19.670 --> 05:21.969
My youth has been restored.

05:21.970 --> 05:23.090
Furthermore!

05:23.680 --> 05:28.310
I've secured the help of the local modeling
agency where Super Sonico works.

05:29.010 --> 05:33.140
Allow me to introduce
model Ouka Satsurikuin!

05:33.940 --> 05:38.650
How do you do?! I'm Ouka,
the famed bikini model!

05:39.400 --> 05:44.240
I will literally break a leg to help
the shopping arcade boost its sales!

05:45.410 --> 05:48.530
What about hiring some college kids
to help out part time?

05:48.700 --> 05:50.500
Yeah, there are lots
of cute girls on campus.

05:50.790 --> 05:53.160
Why are you ignoring me?!

05:53.710 --> 05:57.669
S-Suzu, are we really
supposed to wear these clothes?

05:57.670 --> 05:58.789
Of course.

05:58.790 --> 06:03.669
But it's December. I think it's too
cold out for us to wear these.

06:03.670 --> 06:07.550
Nico... Fuuri... This is all
for the shopping district!

06:07.930 --> 06:13.020
Incidentally, I have to work at SuperNova, so I
can only show up here at night. But good luck!

06:13.310 --> 06:16.020
Come on! Suzu!

06:16.480 --> 06:19.520
You'll have all the meat buns
you can eat on your breaks.

06:20.400 --> 06:21.899
I'll do my best!

06:21.900 --> 06:23.940
F-Fuuri...

06:24.280 --> 06:29.950
Then it's settled. The Musatani Shopping
District launches Operation: Santa Girl tomorrow!

06:30.120 --> 06:32.040
YEAH!

06:33.200 --> 06:34.790
So, are we all clear?

06:35.370 --> 06:39.790
Being a Santa Girl isn't just wearing a
costume and acting like a normal shop girl.

06:40.340 --> 06:40.960
There.

06:41.170 --> 06:42.050
Thank you!

06:42.051 --> 06:43.379
Let's give out dazzling smiles
and TOTAL customer service.
Thank you!

06:43.380 --> 06:46.010
Let's give out dazzling smiles
and TOTAL customer service.

06:46.720 --> 06:51.350
Any customer who purchases merchandise
should be escorted to the arcade's exit.

06:52.350 --> 06:56.520
Anyone who orders by phone or
Internet gets free delivery.

06:57.770 --> 06:58.650
Send another girl.

06:58.651 --> 07:00.269
What do you mean by that?!

07:00.270 --> 07:04.430
For
Your
Shopping
Needs
Musatani
Shopping
District

07:05.030 --> 07:07.030
Is it okay to take one of both of you?

07:07.570 --> 07:09.610
Ah, of course!

07:10.820 --> 07:13.700
Anyone with free time will
hand out leaflets at the station.

07:14.200 --> 07:15.870
You'll be greeted by the Santa Girls!

07:16.370 --> 07:18.620
Please visit the Musatani
Shopping District!

07:23.340 --> 07:25.170
This is the Musatani Shopping District...

07:25.760 --> 07:27.260
Welcome!

07:27.550 --> 07:28.905
ZEPPELIN

07:28.720 --> 07:30.260
I'm sorry I'm late.

07:28.906 --> 07:30.260
PUB

07:30.760 --> 07:32.640
How were today's sales?

07:32.970 --> 07:36.600
Overall, we're seein'
sales up by about 30%.

07:36.890 --> 07:39.440
It's a heck of a start, Suzu.

07:39.690 --> 07:41.769
I see. That's great!

07:41.770 --> 07:43.230
But still...

07:43.650 --> 07:45.230
Look at Sonico and the girls.

07:46.360 --> 07:48.899
S-s-so cold!

07:48.900 --> 07:52.029
N-need more calories...

07:52.030 --> 07:54.869
J-joint movement is impeded.

07:54.870 --> 07:57.040
Here. It's hot ginger.

07:58.080 --> 07:59.579
This will warm you up.

07:59.580 --> 08:02.040
The heck?! THIS is the tenacity of youth?!

08:02.380 --> 08:06.380
Easy for you to say, Suzu.
You're not dressed like this.

08:07.010 --> 08:09.469
So you CAN'T tough it out
for the shopping arcade?

08:09.470 --> 08:12.010
Uh, Suzu, you're asking too much...

08:13.010 --> 08:14.509
This is bad, Mr. Tomi!

08:14.510 --> 08:18.270
Those department-store assholes
called in some pop idols to counter us!

08:18.600 --> 08:20.099
Pop idols?!

08:20.100 --> 08:21.100
Yeah.

08:21.190 --> 08:24.900
A really popular group that's
making waves these days:

08:25.360 --> 08:29.780
"Love Idol ABC Forever Mountain 109"!

08:30.740 --> 08:33.110
ABC's really coming HERE?!

08:33.410 --> 08:36.580
Apparently, they're bringing in a roster
of group members that changes daily.

08:36.581 --> 08:41.290
TICKETS
LINE HERE

08:36.990 --> 08:40.910
People are already camping outside
the department store for tickets!

08:41.660 --> 08:45.539
Damn that store. They're
using money to get their way!

08:45.540 --> 08:50.089
The local youngsters have been in a frenzy
ever since they heard about ABC.

08:50.090 --> 08:53.089
Now there's NOTHING we
can do to compete with them!

08:53.090 --> 08:54.590
This is terrible...

08:56.220 --> 08:57.350
Oh, Yasu?

08:57.930 --> 08:59.520
Where are you going?

09:01.770 --> 09:04.849
Ah! My grandpa is on death's door...

09:04.850 --> 09:05.560
Kuni!

09:05.560 --> 09:05.980
Bastard!
Kuni!

09:05.980 --> 09:06.650
Bastard!
Lemme go! YOU'RE a fan of Yuu's, too!

09:06.651 --> 09:09.190
Lemme go! YOU'RE a fan of Yuu's, too!

09:09.940 --> 09:11.399
Yuu!

09:11.400 --> 09:13.990
Speaking of pop idols,
you're looking right at one!

09:14.410 --> 09:16.200
What do we do, Mr. Tomi?

09:16.450 --> 09:22.910
Well, what CAN we do? That store has
way more funds than we do. Suzu?

09:23.410 --> 09:26.000
I'll think of a plan by tomorrow morning.

09:26.790 --> 09:30.549
Nico, Fuuri. Handle
things in the arcade till then.

09:30.550 --> 09:31.799
R-right.

09:31.800 --> 09:33.010
Understood!

09:39.430 --> 09:43.020
A-all our customers are gone...

09:43.480 --> 09:47.730
That's the Idol Effect.
It can reduce things to THIS overnight.

09:48.570 --> 09:52.190
At this rate, there's no
hope anymore, is there?

09:52.610 --> 09:54.239
Come on, Ouka.

09:54.240 --> 09:56.199
We can't just give up.

09:56.200 --> 09:57.200
Indeed.

09:58.580 --> 10:00.580
It's too soon to quit!

10:01.290 --> 10:02.290
Suzu!

10:02.660 --> 10:04.620
I stayed up thinking things over.

10:05.620 --> 10:11.210
If that department store has stolen our young male
customers, then we'll just draw in the FEMALE ones!

10:11.710 --> 10:16.009
We need to recruit some pretty boys
to form a Handsome Santa Brigade, and...

10:16.010 --> 10:18.009
Emergency! Mr. Tomi!

10:18.010 --> 10:20.590
FISH

10:18.600 --> 10:20.589
The fish seller! What's wrong?

10:20.590 --> 10:20.720
FISH

10:21.100 --> 10:23.730
That damn department store called
MORE friggin' pop idols!

10:25.140 --> 10:26.520
Men, this time...

10:27.440 --> 10:30.610
the popular foreign group Dimension 3!

10:31.190 --> 10:32.729
Huh? No way!

10:32.730 --> 10:34.400
D3 is coming?

10:34.650 --> 10:37.840
Yeah. All the female customers
in the district are goin' nuts!

10:37.841 --> 10:39.150
GIANT
DEPARTMENT

10:38.030 --> 10:41.240
That department store's
sucking them in left and right!

10:41.620 --> 10:49.620
FISH

10:42.540 --> 10:47.120
How could a single Japanese department
store bring in a foreign pop group?!

10:47.670 --> 10:50.080
I doubt that they could turn a profit.

10:50.380 --> 10:52.270
Well, for every 500 yen you spend there,

10:52.271 --> 10:54.919
Christmas Campaign
Collect point to meet D3!

10:52.460 --> 10:56.920
They give you a stamp. If you get 100 points,
they'll let you into a meet-and-greet!

10:54.920 --> 10:59.050
You've collected 100 point!
Congratulations!!

10:57.260 --> 10:59.050
What? A-a hundred points?!

10:59.430 --> 11:05.220
In other words, 50,000 yen!
Those greedy department store bastards!

11:05.600 --> 11:07.140
You going somewhere?

11:07.520 --> 11:08.480
To, um...

11:08.481 --> 11:09.599
The bathroom.

11:09.600 --> 11:11.520
Wait right there!

11:12.320 --> 11:13.609
WHERE ARE YOU GOING?!

11:13.610 --> 11:15.439
I'm a fan of Andy's!

11:15.440 --> 11:17.200
I want to meet Frank!

11:17.360 --> 11:18.859
Andy!

11:18.860 --> 11:20.410
Frank!

11:20.950 --> 11:24.579
So... What will happen
to the shopping arcade?

11:24.580 --> 11:26.200
Could it be all over?

11:26.790 --> 11:28.329
Sonico! A customer.

11:28.330 --> 11:30.170
Ah! O-okay!

11:30.920 --> 11:32.540
Sorry for the wait.

11:33.170 --> 11:36.630
You look like you're having a tough time,
but hang in there, Sonico.

11:37.010 --> 11:38.340
R-right!

11:40.010 --> 11:42.220
What's wrong, Ayaka?

11:43.260 --> 11:48.140
Apparently, a kindergarten friend of hers told
her yesterday that there's no Santa Claus.

11:49.020 --> 11:51.310
But there is! Daddy said so!

11:51.730 --> 11:56.530
He said there's a real Santa!
You think so too, don't you, Sonico?!

11:56.860 --> 11:58.739
Of... Of course.

11:58.740 --> 12:00.490
You bet there is!

12:00.610 --> 12:02.159
S-Suzu!

12:02.160 --> 12:06.330
Santa Claus is for real.
And I just had a thought!

12:06.660 --> 12:10.370
This idea will turn things around and save
the Musatani Shopping District!

12:10.790 --> 12:11.790
Huh?

12:12.730 --> 12:17.040
Shopping District Profit Report

12:22.800 --> 12:24.260
HUH?!

12:23.070 --> 12:24.260
- Christmas Operations Center
- Musatani Shopping District Office

12:24.720 --> 12:26.420
Call in a real Santa Claus?!

12:26.421 --> 12:27.769
Christmas Santa Campaign

12:27.770 --> 12:28.980
Yes, that's right.

12:29.310 --> 12:31.100
What're you talking about, Suzu?

12:31.390 --> 12:33.649
There's no way a "real" Santa Claus exist...

12:33.650 --> 12:36.609
No, he DOES. Please look at this.

12:36.610 --> 12:38.400
World Santa Association

12:37.400 --> 12:41.070
Qualifications for Being an Officially Recognized
Santa of the World Santa Claus Association:

12:37.440 --> 12:40.239
"World Santa Claus Association"?

12:40.240 --> 12:41.240
Yes.

12:41.610 --> 12:44.280
And its members are...

12:44.910 --> 12:49.250
That's right! They're recognized by
the Association as genuine Santas!

12:50.040 --> 12:53.170
Suzu, are you suggesting we contact them...

12:53.580 --> 12:55.920
and request a Santa Claus to come here?

12:56.250 --> 13:01.469
Of course! The department may steal your young
customers, but if we bring in a real Santa Claus,

13:01.470 --> 13:03.929
it will draw parents AND their kids
back to the shopping arcade!

13:03.930 --> 13:05.220
That makes sense.

13:05.470 --> 13:07.220
Good idea, Suzu!

13:08.600 --> 13:09.769
Yeah, but still...

13:09.770 --> 13:11.850
How are we gonna get Santa to come here?

13:12.020 --> 13:14.180
<i>Hi. This is Leyla.</i>

13:14.310 --> 13:20.020
<i>"Could you send Santa
Claus to out shopping district?"</i>

13:20.150 --> 13:23.400
<i>"Do it, even if you can't. Or I
will make you very troubled."</i>

13:23.490 --> 13:24.609
Grandma...

13:24.610 --> 13:26.780
Her English is so great!

13:28.280 --> 13:30.950
They said Santa Claus will come.

13:32.160 --> 13:33.960
Leyla's incredible, all right!

13:34.250 --> 13:37.040
Nice! Operation: Real-Live Santa...

13:37.380 --> 13:38.880
will now begin!

13:40.250 --> 13:42.210
Meet the Real Santa Claus!

13:42.670 --> 13:46.800
The real Santa Claus is coming to
the Musatani Shopping District!

13:47.260 --> 13:50.929
He'll be giving out lots
of presents for the kids.

13:50.930 --> 13:54.770
When you think "shopping," think the
Musatani Shopping District!

13:58.270 --> 13:59.730
Wow...

14:00.230 --> 14:01.900
We got all our foot traffic back!

14:02.490 --> 14:05.740
The "Santa Claus Effect"
really is powerful, huh?

14:06.070 --> 14:07.110
Also...

14:07.410 --> 14:09.330
Look at all them young customers!

14:09.660 --> 14:11.990
Mr. Tomi! Great news!

14:12.120 --> 14:16.080
That foreign boy band the department
store hired has cancelled!

14:16.330 --> 14:17.040
Really?!

14:17.330 --> 14:20.630
It seems there was a
problem with the contract.

14:20.840 --> 14:24.720
Now they're so packed with angry customers
that they can't sell anything!

14:25.050 --> 14:32.349
Also, when Sonico's talent manager went to go check
on things, he was a hit with the foreign tourists!

14:32.350 --> 14:34.810
Oh! Fantastic, samurai!

14:35.140 --> 14:35.890
No!

14:35.891 --> 14:38.809
Ninja? Noh? Kyogen? Kabuki?

14:38.810 --> 14:39.810
Not at all!

14:41.070 --> 14:43.279
Fortune's smiling on us, Mr. Tomi.

14:43.280 --> 14:47.530
Yeah. All that's left is to wait for
the real Santa to show up.

14:49.740 --> 14:51.910
Thank you very much!

14:52.490 --> 14:55.290
Hey, when is Santa coming?

14:56.460 --> 15:01.170
They say he comes on Christmas Eve.
Look forward to it, okay?

15:01.880 --> 15:02.880
Yeah!

15:05.720 --> 15:08.510
Suzu's idea was a huge success!

15:13.560 --> 15:14.600
Ayaka.

15:16.560 --> 15:21.020
What's wrong? You're not with your mother?

15:23.730 --> 15:29.530
Oh, Ayaka! The real Santa Claus is
coming to the shopping district.

15:29.860 --> 15:32.819
What your daddy told you was true, so...

15:32.820 --> 15:34.450
Ayaka

15:32.950 --> 15:34.450
He's a liar.

15:36.000 --> 15:38.830
But Santa really is coming.

15:39.120 --> 15:42.790
Daddy said he'd be back
from overseas on Christmas...

15:43.590 --> 15:51.590
But he's a liar. If he lied about that, he's
lied about everything! There is no Santa Claus!

15:52.390 --> 15:53.470
Ayaka...

15:54.810 --> 15:57.480
Ayaka! There you are.

15:57.890 --> 15:59.520
I'm sorry, Sonico.

15:59.770 --> 16:01.059
Not at all.

16:01.060 --> 16:03.019
Well, let's go home.

16:03.020 --> 16:04.859
No! I won't!

16:04.860 --> 16:06.319
Don't be selfish.

16:06.320 --> 16:07.779
No!

16:07.780 --> 16:08.950
Come on, hold still!

16:11.740 --> 16:15.740
Ah, Sonico. I look forward
to the event. Good luck.

16:15.990 --> 16:19.250
R-right. Thank you very much!

16:20.210 --> 16:22.380
Don't run off like that again.

16:28.760 --> 16:32.640
Grandma. Isn't Daddy coming home?

16:33.220 --> 16:35.890
It seems his work is very busy.

16:38.720 --> 16:42.020
What I want for a present is...

16:49.940 --> 16:52.780
At last, we meet a real Santa Claus.

16:52.990 --> 16:55.779
Y-yes. I'm getting nervous.

16:55.780 --> 16:57.410
Oh! Looks like he's here!

16:59.620 --> 17:02.370
W-welcome, Santa Claus!

17:02.620 --> 17:03.919
Ho, ho, ho!

17:03.920 --> 17:05.789
My name is Tomi!

17:05.790 --> 17:08.880
Thank you so much for coming for me.

17:10.090 --> 17:12.130
Y-you speak Japanese?

17:12.590 --> 17:15.720
Yes, I own a residence here.

17:17.970 --> 17:22.230
We're sorry for the short notice.
Thank you so much for coming!

17:22.690 --> 17:28.019
Not at all. The event venue is close
to home, so it worked out fine.

17:28.020 --> 17:31.070
Oh! So you're a local?

17:32.190 --> 17:33.239
That's right.

17:33.240 --> 17:37.370
So, Santa, what made
you decide to be a Santa?

17:38.030 --> 17:42.500
The truth is, I told my daughter
that Santa Claus was real.

17:43.330 --> 17:49.250
I don't want to be a liar, so while I was overseas,
I took the Santa Claus Certification Exam.

17:49.550 --> 17:53.220
That's so wonderful!
Your daughter will be...

17:54.550 --> 17:55.720
U-um!

17:56.300 --> 17:57.300
What is it?

17:57.390 --> 17:59.680
C-could you be...?

18:00.770 --> 18:02.140
Uh, everyone?

18:02.730 --> 18:05.140
Santa Claus will be arriving shortly.

18:05.600 --> 18:08.899
Have you all thought about
what presents you want?

18:08.900 --> 18:11.529
YES!

18:11.530 --> 18:16.700
We asked the mothers what their kids wanted
ahead of time, then got everything ready.

18:17.570 --> 18:21.909
The presents are numbered,
so please pass them out in order.

18:21.910 --> 18:23.869
Ho, ho, ho! Okay.

18:23.870 --> 18:25.660
Thank you very much.

18:25.790 --> 18:29.630
Okay, here he is: Santa Claus!

18:30.460 --> 18:32.000
Ho, ho, ho!

18:33.090 --> 18:36.930
Santa will be giving you
your presents in order!

18:39.800 --> 18:41.970
Present for you.

18:42.260 --> 18:43.890
Thank you, Santa!

18:44.270 --> 18:45.430
Ho, ho, ho.

18:45.560 --> 18:47.979
Wow! It's the doll I wanted!

18:47.980 --> 18:49.310
A helicopter!

18:49.560 --> 18:50.939
This is great.

18:50.940 --> 18:54.570
Suzu's plan is a HUGE success, huh?

18:54.990 --> 18:57.400
By the way, where's Sonico?

18:57.820 --> 18:59.820
Ah. Well, she...

19:00.490 --> 19:02.910
She's being a real Santa Claus herself.

19:10.630 --> 19:12.210
Oh, my. Sonico.

19:12.420 --> 19:16.340
I-I'm sorry! Um, is Ayaka here?

19:17.090 --> 19:19.390
Well, she won't come out of her room...

19:19.890 --> 19:22.390
Would you mind calling her?

19:22.930 --> 19:24.140
Please!

19:25.350 --> 19:27.310
Present for you.

19:28.730 --> 19:32.270
Ayaka. That's the real Santa Claus there.

19:33.360 --> 19:35.110
It's Santa?

19:36.030 --> 19:37.860
Let's go, Ayaka.

19:38.490 --> 19:44.160
I'm sure he's brought you the
present you want more than anything.

19:44.740 --> 19:45.740
Really?

19:46.120 --> 19:49.000
Santa Claus would never lie.

19:54.130 --> 19:55.919
Present for you.

19:55.920 --> 19:57.720
Thank you, Santa!

19:58.380 --> 19:59.720
Ho, ho, ho.

20:04.510 --> 20:09.190
Santa Claus! There's a present I want.

20:09.640 --> 20:11.520
They say you brought it for me.

20:16.280 --> 20:18.360
Close your eyes.

20:22.950 --> 20:24.950
Please open your eyes.

20:30.620 --> 20:32.330
Santa Claus?

20:34.250 --> 20:35.250
Ayaka.

20:37.670 --> 20:39.969
D-Daddy!

20:39.970 --> 20:41.429
Sorry I'm so late.

20:41.430 --> 20:45.890
It was great! The real Santa was
here, Daddy, just like you said!

20:46.470 --> 20:48.970
And he made my wish come true!

20:49.640 --> 20:52.560
Really? That's wonderful, Ayaka.

20:53.350 --> 20:54.350
Daddy!

20:54.440 --> 20:55.810
This really is...

20:56.730 --> 20:58.190
a wonderful Christmas.

21:00.150 --> 21:07.030
Shiroi yuki ga machi o tsutsundeku
White snow envelops the town

21:07.700 --> 21:09.080
Holy night

21:09.750 --> 21:15.130
Konya toiki wa wata no you
Tonight, our breaths are like cotton

21:15.290 --> 21:18.420
Omoi, todoke
I want my feelings to reach you

21:19.130 --> 21:22.300
Kimi mo miteru ka na
Are you watching, too?

21:23.130 --> 21:24.590
Holy night

21:24.840 --> 21:30.310
Hitori, onaji sora no shita
Alone, under the same sky

21:30.980 --> 21:34.650
SENTIMENTAL na kane no oto
The sentimental sound of the bells

21:34.980 --> 21:38.690
Mune o kyun to shimetsukeru yo
My heart lightens up

21:39.440 --> 21:43.860
Rainen wa kanaetai
I want next year's wish to come true

21:46.120 --> 21:49.080
Christmas Eve

21:49.790 --> 21:53.290
Chotto tereru kedo
I'm a little shy, but

21:53.620 --> 21:57.210
Ai o utaou, kanadeyou
I'll play and sing of love

21:57.500 --> 22:00.710
Kimi dake ni Just for you

22:01.840 --> 22:08.890
Very merry Christmastime song for you

22:09.350 --> 22:16.900
VERY MERRY CHRISTMAS kirameku
Very merry Christmas sparkling

22:17.730 --> 22:23.530
Taisetsu na koto wa onaji kisetsu o
What's important is that the two of us

22:23.860 --> 22:29.990
Futari de tsugosu koto da ne
Pass the same seasons together

22:30.450 --> 22:33.039
Here's to the victory
of the shopping district!

22:33.040 --> 22:38.710
Rainen wa kimi to futarikiri de
Next year, I want the two of us

22:33.500 --> 22:35.330
Cheers!

22:37.080 --> 22:40.480
Huh. So that happened, too? That was
pretty thoughtful of you, Nico.

22:40.481 --> 22:45.470
Te o tsunaide arukitai
To walk alone together, hand in hand

22:42.340 --> 22:46.260
Honestly, I wanted him to go back
home with Ayaka right away...

22:47.130 --> 22:51.720
But he said he couldn't
abandon his duty as Santa.

23:02.690 --> 23:08.110
Still, Ayaka's wish came
true. That's great, Nico.

23:08.320 --> 23:09.320
Yup!

23:12.580 --> 23:13.580
Snow!

23:15.410 --> 23:17.459
A White Christmas, huh?

23:17.460 --> 23:18.460
Yes.

23:20.130 --> 23:21.840
Merry Christmas!

23:22.040 --> 23:23.040
Yes.

23:25.050 --> 23:33.050
Next Episode Preview

23:25.420 --> 23:26.759
First Astronomical Velocity's...

23:26.760 --> 23:28.129
New Year's show is set!

23:28.130 --> 23:29.130
And it's called:

23:29.300 --> 23:30.800
"Super Supernova"!

23:31.300 --> 23:32.300
Love and peace...

23:32.301 --> 23:33.389
And rock-n-roll.

23:33.390 --> 23:35.140
We'll try hard to bring all these to you!

23:35.350 --> 23:37.310
Next time, "I'm Right Hear!"

23:37.311 --> 23:40.060
I'm Right Hear!

23:37.600 --> 23:39.480
Let's do this, guys!
